cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this independent verification, please cite it as below, AND cite
  the original theorem and Lean formalization by Claude / Anthropic.
title: >-
  Independent third-party verification of the Lean formalization of
  "More Than Two Thirds of the Zeros of the Riemann Zeta Function Lie on the
  Critical Line"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Riemann Labs (primaryhosting)"
abstract: >-
  An independent, third-party replication and dual-kernel verification of the
  Lean 4 formalization accompanying an AI-authored (Claude / Anthropic) proof
  that at least 2/3 (more precisely, an improvement of the proven lower bound
  from 41.6% to 67.2%) of the nontrivial zeros of the Riemann zeta function lie
  on the critical line. The formalization was rebuilt from its pinned toolchain
  in independent CI (9,010-job lake build), audited to depend only on Lean's
  three standard axioms with zero sorryAx across 42 headline statements, and
  replayed through both the Lean kernel and the independent nanoda kernel via
  the leanprover/comparator tool. This is a proportion result and is NOT a proof
  of the Riemann Hypothesis; the theorem and its Lean proof are the work of
  Claude / Anthropic, not of the verifier.
date-released: "2026-08-11"
version: "1.0.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://github.com/primaryhosting/zeta-two-thirds-verification"
